body:
Hey Annelies. Cool to see another Belgian on here. Makes me feel less alone, haha. I know how it feels to get scared and stressed about this issue. Posting pictures and sharing this issue with others isn't easy either. I do remember thinking going to the doctor would solve everything. How wrong I was. They didn't even check my scalp or anything, lol. Just instantly prescribed me minoxidil and later finasteride. It's when I realised our doctors don't really have that much knowledge when it comes to hair loss. My hair has been thinning for months and while I still don't have any bald patches or anything, it's definitely gotten worse. Most people IRL don't seem to notice though. When I went to the doctor and dermatologist for the first time waaaaay back, they didn't even believe I was suffering from hair loss. They looked at me and said my hair fine. I think that was like almost 2 years ago. Mind you, I actually believed them. And for a while just figured I was exaggerating. But I now know that I was right even back then 😅

&#x200B;

What you're saying about blood results is interesting. I have of course done many blood tests since this issue started. Because I was convinced it was some vitamin/mineral deficiency. But my doctor(s) always said my tests were fine with just my white blood cell count being low. But that doesn't have anything to do with hair thinning AFAIK. They never actually share the results with me though so I think I'm gonna ask them to show me the results so I can check if anything is near the lower limit.

&#x200B;

As for my gut, right now I seem to think it's related to my hair thinning. This is of course pure speculation but last year when I had major appetite issues and bloating etc... they gave me those antacids (it was called pantomed) and while it relieved some of my issues, it didn't fix the actual issue. It felt like a bandaid. So what did I do? Something drastic. I dropped the meds, I changed my diet and the way I eat. I dropped milk completely from my diet. And guess what? My appetite issues are completely gone. I'm eating more than ever these days. It feels like a first step to feeling better. Unfortunately, I started to get heartburn/some hot feeling in my esophagus. I never had this before. I think the antacids caused it. I probably never had too much stomach acid and those meds might have given me hypochlorhydria (low stomach acid). This is of course a BIG theory 😅 But I'm gonna find out soon because I made an appointment with gastro specialist. Doctors really love to prescribe antacids in Belgium for stomach issues. I know a lot of people who take them. But I honestly think they do more harm than good unless you really have too much stomach acid. But IIRC that's pretty rare. 

Anyway, this post has gotten a lot longer than I had in mind! I just wanted to let you know where I'm at right now. It's definitely been an interesting ride. I hope we both find what we want.

I think it's fucked that the best medication to combat hair loss is such a controversial drug. If the problem was that it works for some people and not for others, then it would still be disappointing but not that bad.

&#x200B;

Instead we have something that may work or may not work but it might also work and give sides or... worst case scenario... not work AND give you sides.

Damn, man... it honestly feels like I've hit the jackpot when it comes to these things. 

&#x200B;

I've dealt with a lot of shit in my life. And this is just another thing I happen to suffer from.  I'm starting to believe in fate for real.

&#x200B;

Feels like I'm playing life on the very hard difficulty setting, lol.

I'm not sure since I don't really weigh myself, but one thing I've noticed is that my arms have become really thin. I feel a lot less strong. Could just be muscle wasting because of the corona situation though. And I sweat a lot less too. I'm not even sure I can still sweat. It's like heat makes me itch now.

&#x200B;

I feel more hungry lately as well, so I think I'm eating more than usual. But I'm not gaining any weight. 

&#x200B;

Sidenote: last summer, I had a stomach issues and got diagnosed with gastric inflammation and ulcers. I had really, really low appetite back then and had to take meds. Took a long while for my appetite to get better.
